How the model weights (drama3-small-IQ3_XXS.gguf, downloaded separately) were modified:
- Routed experts were pruned per layer using speech-calibrated routing statistics. Layers 0, 1, 2
  and 36 keep all 256 experts; every other layer keeps 100 or 101 of 256 (4,640 of 10,240 expert
  slots). Routers were cut to the kept rows.
- The kept experts were quantized to IQ3_XXS using an importance matrix from speech calibration
  data. The dense backbone (attention / Gated DeltaNet), the embeddings and the multi-token audio
  tower were quantized to Q8_0. The codec weights are unchanged (F16).
- The output head was reduced to the EOS row plus the 4,096 semantic-token rows (speech only).
- Routers and shared experts were refit layer by layer against the original model's activations.
- The result was distilled from the original model for 100 optimizer steps on Japanese and English
  speech. Rank-64 LoRA updates of the attention and Gated DeltaNet projections were merged into the
  weights; routers, shared experts, norms and the speech head were updated directly.

How the code in drama3_torch/ relates to the Fish Audio Materials:
- model.py, codec.py and text.py reimplement the Drama 3 model, codec and prompt format from
  fish-speech (github.com/fishaudio/fish-speech, commit 1ff3c3e, files
  models/text2semantic/fish_omni/*, models/dac/{modded_dac,rvq}.py, configs/modded_dac_vq.yaml).
  Changes: weights are read from the GGUF and kept quantized (Q8_0 / IQ3_XXS) with fused
  dequantizing matmul kernels; per-layer expert counts and the speech-only head are supported;
  the codec runs with folded weight normalization, without the descript-audio-codec / audiotools
  packages, in chunks; decoding uses static buffers and CUDA graphs.
- generate.py follows the sampler of the audio.cpp fish_drama3 port (github.com/JarodMica/audio.cpp)
  and adds drama3-small's pause fix (silence-code masking with a per-take adaptive silence list,
  and a length guard). silence_codes.json was derived from drama3-small's own renders.

